  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic, the JSB grammar at high flow. The end connection ladder runs to DN25 forms, the letters shedding their footnote superscripts as on the JSB. The o-ring and trim position pairs a USP o-ring with the 6L trim, the 2-series rows self-relieving; two of those rows print Releiving, the sheet's own spelling. The trim position's dual Cv labels, 1.5 on the half inch and 1.9 above, ride the labels. The inlet gauge ladder prints plain zeros on this sheet, no slashed glyphs. The outlet gauge non-standard row prints ZZ though the position is single width, carried as printed.",
